 "result": "I created two files in the repository root: `Dockerfile` and `.dockerignore`. I could not build or run the image, so it is unverified.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`**: a two-stage build. The builder is `golang:1.27-bookworm` and compiles `wings` with `CGO_ENABLED=0`, using the Makefile's flags plus a `VERSION` build arg. The runtime is `debian:bookworm-slim` with `ca-certificates` and `tzdata`. The entrypoint is `/usr/local/bin/wings`, which uses its default config path, `/etc/pelican/config.yml`. Ports 8080 and 2022 are exposed.\n- **`.dockerignore`**: keeps `.git`, build outputs, logs, vendored code, and the Nix/Makefile files out of the build context. It also excludes `config*.yml`/`config*.yaml` so node tokens and other secrets don't end up in the build context.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n\n- **Go version:** `go.mod` requires Go 1.27.4, but `flake.nix` pins 1.22. I followed `go.mod`. I could not confirm that the `golang:1.27-bookworm` tag exists, so if the build fails at the `FROM` line, that tag is the first thing to check.\n- **Runs as root:** Wings needs the Docker socket and manages files owned by other users, so I did not add a `USER`.\n- **No startup script:** Wings creates its own directories, so a script wasn't needed. The config file is not baked into the image; it has to be bind-mounted.\n- **Host paths must match:** Wings passes its data directories to the host Docker daemon as bind-mount sources. So the host paths `/var/lib/pelican` and the others must be mounted at the same paths in the container. The run example and the notes at the bottom of the Dockerfile cover this.",
